edia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Boron-trifluoride-pi-bonding-2D.png/500px-Boron-trifluoride-pi-bonding-2D.png","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Boron-trifluoride-pi-bonding-2D.png/1280px-Boron-trifluoride-pi-bonding-2D.png","w":893,"h":1100,"caption":{"es":null,"en":"Boron (III) trifluoride structure, showing \"empty\" boron p orbital in pi-type coordinate covalent bonds"},"artist":"Ben Mills","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boron-trifluoride-pi-bonding-2D.png"},{"file":"File:Deltahedral-borane-cluster-array-numbered-3D-bs-17.png","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Deltahedral-borane-cluster-array-numbered-3D-bs-17.png/500px-Deltahedral-borane-cluster-array-numbered-3D-bs-17.png","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Deltahedral-borane-cluster-array-numbered-3D-bs-17.png/1280px-Deltahedral-borane-cluster-array-numbered-3D-bs-17.png","w":3478,"h":7958,"caption":{"es":null,"en":"Ball-and-stick models showing the structures of the boron skeletons of borane clusters. The structures can be rationalised by polyhedral skeletal electron pair theory."},"artist":"Ben Mills","license":"Public domain","licenseUrl":null,"page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deltahedral-borane-cluster-array-numbered-3D-bs-17.png"},{"file":"File:Borfig11a.png","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Borfig11a.png/500px-Borfig11a.png","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Borfig11a.png/1280px-Borfig11a.png","w":1600,"h":2453,"caption":{"es":null,"en":"Unit cell of B4C. The green sphere and icosahedra consist of boron atoms, and black spheres are carbon atoms."},"artist":"Materialscientist","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Borfig11a.png"},{"file":"File:Magnesium-diboride-3D-balls.png","thumb":"ht